WEBVTT

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.940
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.440
They say there's a <i>yokai</i>.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.450
My mom's dead.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.070
Don't tell Kitaro.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.740
I wanna eat something better.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.170
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.970
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.460
OBEBE SWAMP

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:44.550
CHAPTER 18

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:49.470
KAWAUSO'S LIE

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.750
Here it is again, Dad.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:58.790
Hmm. Who could it be doing this?

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.340
What's wrong?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.380
Catchick.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.880
It's this.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.840
They're just vegetables.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.240
Recently they've been
showing up almost every day.

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.810
Huh. From whom?

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.260
We have absolutely no idea.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.400
Why don't you just take them?

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.730
They look tasty.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:24.380
They do look good.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.490
Oh, do you want some?

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.440
Huh?!

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.110
I-I don't need any!

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.070
How come?

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.860
How come? I-I'm on a diet!

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.950
Huh?

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.770
What is it, Kitaro?

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:44.210
Well, I figure, if she's on a diet,
then wouldn't it be better to eat some?

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:45.340
They're vegetables.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:48.110
Cabbage might be good for her.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.760
After so long, it's our summer home!

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.600
It's really been a while.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.620
Thanks to somebody being busy with work.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.390
-That's what a summer home is.
-I know!

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.320
I'm sending these to Cat-san!

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.940
Cat-san? Is that a friend?

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:09.860
Yup!

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:15.950
Cat-san is always wonderful and pretty
and cool and strong,

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:20.620
yet she's kind and so stylish!

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.500
How are things?

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:29.420
Oh, they're all growing healthily.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.680
These are impressive.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.310
Your pure heart must be
reaching the vegetables.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:40.180
I'm really glad you came.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:45.560
I'm really grateful that you let me have
lots of harvested vegetables, too.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:51.570
It's nothing. Without care, a field will
go to shambles in no time.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:55.840
That field didn't have
anyone to take over.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:00.540
I feel really bad
having you do everything...

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:05.000
Please don't. I like doing farm work.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.250
Besides, having someone
eat the food I've grown

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.570
makes me really happy.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:17.840
My wife would often
say things like that, too...

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.150
Oh! What's wrong?!

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.370
Are you okay?

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:43.160
I'm so hungry I felt weak.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.000
What?

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.080
I haven't eaten anything in three days...

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.580
How come?

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:54.050
I have to work as hard as I can
to feed my young little sister.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.680
What about your father and mother?

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.430
My mom's dead.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:02.450
My dad is always out and about playing.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.370
Oh, hold on!

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:10.080
You're just a child,
yet you have it so hard...

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.990
It's not much, but here, take these.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.150
Really?!

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.400
Sure.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:19.660
You need to eat well, too.
Not just your sister.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.510
Thanks!

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:33.710
Today's bath is a corn tea bath
I made from corn silk.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:33.650
-<i>"I'm at my summer home!"</i>
-<i>"Nice!!"</i>

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:36.720
Huh. It smells nice.

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:36.650
<i>"That's nice.
I go to the mountains a lot recently."</i>

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:40.930
By the way, Kitaro, I noticed
the vegetables didn't show up today.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.720
You're right.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.600
I wonder what that was about?

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.810
Who knows?

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:47.980
It must be a day off, that's all.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:51.860
Or was there some vegetable
that you wanted to eat?

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:55.860
I'm not sure. I guess I'm in
the mood for sweet potatoes.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:59.490
Sweet potatoes?
It's a little early for those...

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:00.900
Huh? What's wrong?

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.110
N-Nothing!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.470
Good night!

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.710
Ow, ow, ow...

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.130
Maybe they're still too small after all...

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:16.570
Oh well.

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:20.220
I'm taking a walk!

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.100
Daddy is too!

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:22.930
Seriously?

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:23.890
What?!

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:26.100
-Sure!
-You're too kind!

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.890
Hey! Don't we have to clean first today?

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:30.190
Seriously?

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:33.600
It's dusty inside
and the grass needs trimming.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.910
They say there's a <i>yokai</i> around here.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:41.650
A-A <i>yokai</i>?!

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.830
Especially in
the swamp called Obebe Swamp,

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:50.600
they say there's a
really crafty <i>yokai</i> living there.

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:54.560
Mana, let's all work on cleaning together!

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.380
Wait. Huh?

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:57.800
Mana! Honestly!

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.470
Don't go too far!

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:01.510
Okay!

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.680
Whew!

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:12.850
Come to think of it, didn't Cat-san say
she goes to the mountains?

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.220
I wonder why?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.500
Maybe for picnics?

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.840
How nice!

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:26.260
That's the problem with the mountains.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:27.570
Huh?

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:36.210
Heave ho! Heave ho!

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:41.990
Mana?

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:44.820
Cat-san?!

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:48.530
What a surprise, seeing you here.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.640
Yes. I was...

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.040
surprised, too...

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:59.740
Uh, are you changing your image?
It looks good.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:04.280
Oh, these are work clothes.
They're the best to move around in.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:08.080
Unfortunately,
it's not very fashionable...

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.290
Oh...

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:14.790
I came here the other day running
an errand for Sand Witch.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:18.540
There was an old man collapsed in a field.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.760
Are you all right?

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.090
That old man

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:27.820
slipped and fell off a cliff with his wife
a few days earlier.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:34.140
The old man was rescued,
but his wife is still missing...

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.440
I couldn't just leave him.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.820
That explains the work pants...

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:40.650
-Huh?
-Oh, nothing!

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.400
That's why you were
helping with the field.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:44.630
Yeah.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:48.160
But, don't tell Kitaro about this.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.330
Huh? Why not?

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:51.700
Because!

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.850
You're going that way, right Mana?

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.580
I'm glad I saw you. Bye.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:59.120
Oh, um, Cat-san!

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:03.960
Uh, well... See you tomorrow.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:13.070
It's a nice story,

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.790
but my image of Cat-san...

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:24.590
Miss!

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:26.590
You again!

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:29.120
Did you enjoy the vegetables?

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:32.320
They were delicious!
Or so I'd like to say...

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:36.290
My dad came home and ate them all...

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:37.670
I see...

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:41.040
I don't care how hungry I am.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.340
But I feel sorry for my
poor little brother...

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:45.670
Little brother?

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:48.320
Didn't you say it was your little sister?

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:52.760
I-I've got a brother, too!
I've got lots of siblings!

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:56.310
That's why, as the oldest,
I've gotta be strong!

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:57.560
That sounds hard...

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:02.080
It's not that bad.
I do get a little down sometimes though...

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:07.210
No, I've got my siblings!
I shouldn't feel down!

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.790
Here, take these.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.040
You sure?!

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:16.040
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:19.540
I want the person
who needs these the most to eat them.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:22.940
Thank you, kind miss!

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:35.450
Man, talk about a kind miss.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:12:00.000
Look out! Wild boars are coming!
It's a huge herd!

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.480
What?!

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:08.840
Look at them run!

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:12.780
This is why I just can't
stop teasing humans.

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:18.140
What's wrong? Too scared to move?

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.810
Oh very well.

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:28.300
Don't cry. I'll carry you to your home.

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:38.560
Oh man!

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:43.560
I'm still hungry.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:47.790
OBEBE SWAMP

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:54.950
I wanna eat something better
than just potatoes.

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:05.190
KAWAUSO AND KITARO

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:09.690
<i>YOKAI</i> KAWAUSO

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:08.630
-<i>"No, no."</i>
-<i>"I'll turn this into money."</i>

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:09.630
<i>"Sorry."</i>

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:14.780
Kitaro, there was a letter
in the Yokai Mailbox.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:16.780
A letter?

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:21.750
You're doing field work again today?

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:25.580
Yeah. I thought I'd
harvest the watermelons today.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:30.590
Oh. I didn't know watermelons
don't grow on trees.

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:34.340
Wait, you've never seen
a watermelon grown before?

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:36.750
Most people haven't.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:41.030
Wow, it's heavy! I didn't know
watermelons were this heavy.

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:44.190
You've never held a watermelon either?

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:47.670
We always buy ones that are
cut into small pieces.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.380
I see.

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:58.030
Calm down, it's just a flower chafer.

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:01.780
You're fine with bugs?

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:08.060
It's bugs that carry pollen, making plants
blossom, and making the land fertile.

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:14.670
Trees and flowers and bugs and animals...

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.680
People and <i>yokai</i>...

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:21.070
They're all the same.
Just elements that make up nature.

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:25.890
It looks like humans these days
have been forgetting that.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:30.150
First off...

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:35.460
Try the taste of a freshly picked one.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:37.780
Go ahead.

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:40.030
In that case, here goes.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:49.750
It's delicious! I've never had
a watermelon this good before!

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:55.860
Freshly picked vegetables and fruits are
full of nutrients and really juicy.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:00.680
The earth grows a tiny seed into food.

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:05.230
Farming lets one feel
that great power up close.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:07.930
I think it's really fulfilling work.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:10.170
Cat-san...

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:15.360
Mana, you're not in your house.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.460
This is how you handle seeds.

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:24.100
See?

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:25.500
But...

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.640
Just try it.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.230
Okay.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.310
Huh?

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:35.550
Huh?!

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:37.380
You're terrible, Mana.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:40.130
Hey! Don't laugh at me!

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:45.890
I think it should be around here.

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.390
Hmm, it seems that way.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:52.770
Cat-san?

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:53.820
Shh! Shh!

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.360
Huh? Mana?

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:56.900
Kitaro.

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.780
What are you doing here? Are you alone?

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:03.490
Uh, well, yeah.
I've got a summer home near here.

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:05.830
Huh. What a coincidence.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:08.960
-Why is Kitaro here?
-What are you doing here, Kitaro?

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:14.040
-I can't let Kitaro see me like this!
-There's a swamp near called Obebe Swamp.

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:17.050
There's a <i>yokai</i> called Kawauso
living there.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:18.420
Obebe Swamp?

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:21.050
Is it a really crafty <i>yokai</i>?

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:24.810
Yeah. Apparently it's been
causing trouble recently.

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:26.680
We got a letter.

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:30.690
It usually disguises itself
as a human child.

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:36.780
Then, for sympathy, it says it has no
parents or it's looking after its siblings

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:40.340
and tricks humans into giving it things.

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:48.260
Man, fish taste a lot better
than vegetables.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:51.460
Hello. We meet again.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:53.880
Oh! Miss!

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:58.790
Thanks for the sweet potatoes
the other day! My sick mom was grateful!

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:01.510
Your sick mom?

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:04.340
Yeah! She's feeling
hungry again thanks to--

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:07.560
You said your mother was dead, didn't you?

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:10.010
Huh?! W-Wait, did I say that?

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:14.520
I knew it.
You're the Obebe Swamp Kawauso!

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:17.520
How did you know?! Oops!

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.360
How dare you trick me!

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:24.700
Cat-san?

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:25.650
Ki--

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:27.990
Catchick?

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:30.310
What's with those clothes?

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:32.620
N-No, this is...!

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:34.630
All right, miss.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:37.290
I'll give back the vegetables you gave,

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:38.880
-so don't be mad.
-Shh! Shh!

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:45.260
She gave me lots of stuff
that she grew herself.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:47.680
Huh. Catchick did?

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.970
Huh? That means...

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:55.890
Catchick, was that your doing?!

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:01.000
This is all...

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:03.340
your fault!

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:05.590
Get back here!

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:09.470
What's going on?

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:11.370
Who knows?

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:15.950
Stop, you!

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:51.490
I was waiting.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:00.020
Stop, damn you!

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.280
Old lady!

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:08.630
Look out!

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.780
You're still running?!

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:14.280
What are you doing here?

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:17.690
I've got you, you dirty <i>yokai</i>!

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:19.480
L-Let go of me!

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:20.870
Michiko!

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:23.230
You're all right!

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:24.840
Darling!

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:28.780
I'm sorry to worry you.

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:32.910
Thank goodness. Thank goodness!

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:35.660
But, how did you survive?

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:39.850
Well, that little boy saved me.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:43.420
Huh?

00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:46.800
Thank you so much.

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:56.730
Ever since I fell down the cliff
and couldn't walk,

00:19:56.730 --> 00:20:00.480
he's been bringing me food
this whole time.

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:05.500
Thanks to him, as you can see, I've
healed enough to where I can walk again.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:07.900
I see.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:11.360
I guess not everything you do is a lie.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:16.990
Nah, that old lady just
ate my table scraps.

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:21.270
I wouldn't care if that old lady died.

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:27.840
In fact, if everybody in this village
disappeared, I'd feel relief.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:34.590
Are you actually lonely?

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:38.790
There's something wrong
with humans these days.

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:43.520
They all abandon the mountains
and the plains and go far away...

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:46.780
Then why don't you stay with--

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:49.500
You could just come with us.

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:52.280
To the GeGeGe Forest.

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:53.130
Huh?

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.410
In the GeGeGe Forest,
you'll have lots of friends.

00:20:56.760 --> 00:21:00.160
I'm sure you won't feel lonely there.

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:03.750
But, I tricked you...

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:10.000
Tricked who? I forgot already.

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:14.010
Thank you.

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:22.100
-You really are so cool, Cat-san!
-What, all of a sudden?!

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:26.650
No matter how you're dressed,
you're still Cat-san!

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:29.690
Why are you stating the obvious?

00:21:29.690 --> 00:21:31.070
By the way,

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:35.030
why did you secretly leave vegetables
in front of our house?

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:38.930
And you acted like
you didn't know anything about it.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:40.530
Th-That's...

00:21:44.310 --> 00:21:46.920
I don't know about any vegetables.

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:50.010
Huh? That wasn't you, Catchick?

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:52.550
I said it wasn't me!

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:54.920
Then who was it?

